@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.6.5
@changelog
  - Codename: My Llama spits Codenames. My Lama not so much.
  - Layers switch Quicks only: Quick 1-3 and the V-POT / Soft 1-5 bank keys edited on Layer 2 or 3 stay on that layer (they were written to Layer 1); editor, right-click menu and tile colours follow the layer the key fires on
  - Startup bank "Use current hardware bank" takes the layer the surface is on under Layers switch Quicks only
  - UC1 input meter skips the audio accessor on tracks with item FX: no more 1-2 s lag on Mixer channel changes and broken-up audio; meter such a track with the Rea-Sixty Input Level JSFX
  - Sleep: letting go of the key that put the surfaces to sleep no longer wakes them
  - RME side-car asks TotalMix for its whole state twice more, 3 s and 10 s after connecting
  - New built-ins (RME): "RME: Ask TotalMix again" and "UF1 Mode: RME" (side-car on / off, as SHIFT + MODE, RME), from any surface and the Stream Deck
  - RME side-car Output page: Crossfeed, Delay, Ref Level, FX Return; Pan stays on the V-Pot above the fader, the extra FX Return page is gone (your own pages stay)
  - TotalMix snapshot and layout keys light in the key's Active / Inactive colours (white when none are set)
  - Known issue: Windows 11 with Smart App Control on refuses to load the unsigned extension ("Bad Image"). Turning Smart App Control off lets it load.
